   "id": "7fPjzCpjiNMJ",
   "from": "Noam Ross",
   "author": "8c8f0ca54c4a2459",
   "date": "2014-09-30T21:39:34Z",
   "subject": "First D-RUG fall meeting: 1:10-3PM Tues, Oct 7",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:1.2;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hello all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">The votes are in, and fall D-RUG sessions will be held <strong>Tuesdays 1:10-3 in Wickson 2124</strong>.  Our <strong>first meeting</strong> will be next week, on Tuesday, <strong>Oct 7</strong>.  </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">For those new to D-RUG, our work sessions are times for you to come to work on your own projects (including classwork) and get help on R and related topics from the D-RUG community.  We have speakers every other week. These talks take up the first hour or less, leaving the rest of the time open for co-work and help. </p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Next week, <a href=\"https://twitter.com/ucdlevy\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://twitter.com/ucdlevy&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468680074000&amp;usg=AOvVaw21dGWMvnA8wzz0CNQYrcRW\">Michael Levy</a> will give a talk on how to use the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">dplyr</code> package to make your R code easier to write and read (and faster, too!).  With <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">dplyr</code>, you can turn this:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;overflow:auto;margin:1em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">crime.by.state &lt;- read.csv(&quot;CrimeStatebyState.csv&quot;)\r\n\r\ncrime.ny.2005 &lt;- crime.by.state[crime.by.state$Year==2005 &amp;\r\n                                  crime.by.state$State==&quot;New York&quot;, \r\n                                c(&quot;Type.of.Crime&quot;, &quot;Count&quot;)]\r\ncrime.ny.2005 &lt;- crime.ny.2005[order(crime.ny.2005$Count, \r\n                                     decreasing=TRUE), ]\r\ncrime.ny.2005$Proportion &lt;- crime.ny.2005$Count /\r\n                            sum(crime.ny.2005$Count)\r\nsummary1 &lt;- aggregate(Count ~ Type.of.Crime,\r\n                      data=crime.ny.2005,\r\n                      FUN=sum)\r\nsummary2 &lt;- aggregate(Count ~ Type.of.Crime,\r\n                      data=crime.ny.2005,\r\n                      FUN=length)\r\nfinal &lt;- merge(summary1, summary2,\r\n               by=&quot;Type.of.Crime&quot;)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">into this: </p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;overflow:auto;margin:1em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">library(dplyr)\r\ncrime.by.state &lt;- read.csv(&quot;CrimeStatebyState.csv&quot;)\r\n\r\nfinal &lt;- crime.by.state %&gt;%\r\n           filter(State==&quot;New York&quot;, Year==2005) %&gt;%\r\n           arrange(desc(Count)) %&gt;%\r\n           select(Type.of.Crime, Count) %&gt;%\r\n           mutate(Proportion=Count/sum(Count)) %&gt;%\r\n           group_by(Type.of.Crime) %&gt;%\r\n           summarise(num.types = n(), counts = sum(Count))\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Much better, no? Michael will show you more!  See you on Tuesday.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Noam</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">*Thanks to <a href=\"http://www.onthelambda.com/2014/02/10/how-dplyr-replaced-my-most-common-r-idioms/\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.onthelambda.com/2014/02/10/how-dplyr-replaced-my-most-common-r-idioms/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468680074000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rsa3My-O21olq7VdcgS6E\">Tony Fischetti for the example</a></p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGVsbG8gYWxsLDxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+VGhlIHZvdGVzIGFyZSBpbiwgYW5kIGZhbGwg\r\nRC1SVUcgc2Vzc2lvbnMgd2lsbCBiZSBoZWxkICoqVHVlc2RheXMgMToxMC0zIGluIFdpY2tzb24g\r\nMjEyNCoqLiZuYnNwOyBPdXIgKipmaXJzdCBtZWV0aW5nKiogd2lsbCBiZSBuZXh0IHdlZWssIG9u\r\nIFR1ZXNkYXksICoqT2N0IDcqKi4gJm5ic3A7PC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5Gb3Ig\r\ndGhvc2UgbmV3IHRvIEQtUlVHLCBvdXIgd29yayBzZXNzaW9ucyBhcmUgdGltZXMgZm9yIHlvdSB0\r\nbyBjb21lIHRvIHdvcmsgb24geW91ciBvd24gcHJvamVjdHMgKGluY2x1ZGluZyB